they became a millionaire,

00:00:40.871 --> 00:00:43.454
no idea, not important to them.

00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:46.351
They remember winning.

00:00:46.351 --> 00:00:50.542
They remember building a
business and being successful.

00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:55.082
Again, the pursuit of freedom
manifests itself in passion.

00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:57.124
That's really what its about.

00:00:57.124 --> 00:00:59.222
- So I just finished the
first chapter of my next book.

00:00:59.222 --> 00:01:00.366
I'm super excited about it.

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:03.956
I'm basically taking the top 500 rules,

00:01:03.956 --> 00:01:05.840
so I'm taking the top 50
people that you guys have

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.353
liked the best from my top 10 rules

00:01:08.353 --> 00:01:10.369
times their 10 rules, we have 500 rules,

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.692
and condensing them down
to the most consistent,

00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:17.321
most common top 10 rules
that everybody has some,

00:01:17.321 --> 00:01:19.330
people who have accomplished
massive success.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.534
And one of the ones that is consistent,

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:24.610
it's the number one rule is
around, following your passion,

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.147
doing the thing that you love.

00:01:26.147 --> 00:01:28.425
And this is not something
new on my channel.

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:30.171
If you've watched Entspressos and Top 10s,

00:01:30.171 --> 00:01:31.333
you've heard this message over

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:32.917
and over and over and over again.

00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.583
- Passion.
- Follow my passion.

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:36.173
- Passion.
- Follow your passion.

00:01:36.173 --> 00:01:37.475
- Recognize your passion.

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:38.556
- Passion.
- Passion

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:39.464
- Passion.

00:01:39.464 --> 00:01:40.645
- Passion.
- Passionate.

00:01:40.645 --> 00:01:41.509
- Passion.
- Passion.

00:01:41.509 --> 00:01:42.342
- Passion.

00:01:42.342 --> 00:01:44.151
- Why I'm really excited
about this one today

00:01:44.151 --> 00:01:46.107
is because it's coming from Kevin O'Leary.

00:01:46.107 --> 00:01:49.289
And Kevin O'Leary, you see
as the Shark on Shark Tank

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:52.139
and always talking about money,
and his goal is making money

00:01:52.139 --> 00:01:54.332
and his goal is sending out his soldiers

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:56.283
to go out and make more
money and come back.

00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:59.268
And his dream is to go
to bed a little richer

00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:01.011
at night than he was
in the morning, right?

00:02:01.011 --> 00:02:02.936
That's all he talks about on Shark Tank

00:02:02.936 --> 00:02:05.550
and in most of his interviews,
and this one was different.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.165
This one was talking about
pursuing your passion.

00:02:08.165 --> 00:02:10.237
This one was talking about him saying

00:02:10.237 --> 00:02:12.466
that most people don't
even remember the day

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:15.334
they became a millionaire
because they were

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.526
doing something much more important.

00:02:17.526 --> 00:02:19.270
And I love hearing that message from him

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.151
because it's atypical from
what you normally hear

00:02:21.151 --> 00:02:22.790
from Kevin O'Leary, but it's true.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.863
The money's important.

00:02:23.863 --> 00:02:24.935
Money's important for everybody.

00:02:24.935 --> 00:02:26.194
Money is important for me.

00:02:26.194 --> 00:02:27.125
I look at my budgets.

00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:28.101
I look at my revenue.

00:02:28.101 --> 00:02:29.253
I look my costs.

00:02:29.253 --> 00:02:30.806
I look at what products are generating

00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:31.903
sales and which ones aren't.

00:02:31.903 --> 00:02:33.749
I look at, for this business, TDS.

00:02:33.749 --> 00:02:35.843
I look at what classes
are generating revenue,

00:02:35.843 --> 00:02:37.010
which ones aren't, how much we

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.190
can pay, how much we can charge.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.703
I look at it constantly.

00:02:39.703 --> 00:02:41.064
It's part of running a business.

00:02:41.064 --> 00:02:42.244
If you are not making money,

00:02:42.244 --> 00:02:43.747
you're going to go out of business.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:45.167
The important thing though is there has

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.703
to be something more important than money.

00:02:47.703 --> 00:02:50.106
Money is number two, might be number three

00:02:50.106 --> 00:02:52.065
or four, but it's not number one.

00:02:52.065 --> 00:02:54.887
If you are in business and
money is number one for you,

00:02:54.887 --> 00:02:56.605
you're not going to have a lot of success.

00:02:56.605 --> 00:02:58.628
There has to be something more important

00:02:58.628 --> 00:03:00.524
that is passionately driving you forward,

00:03:00.524 --> 00:03:02.372
whatever it is, no judgment.

00:03:02.372 --> 00:03:04.380
It could be almost anything.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.987
The thing that you would
do even if you weren't

00:03:05.987 --> 00:03:08.008
getting paid to do, what is that?

00:03:08.008 --> 00:03:09.749
For me, it's helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:09.749 --> 00:03:11.700
I never thought I was going
to make money doing this.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.749
And if you look at a lot of
successful entrepreneurs,

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:16.222
they have no idea how
they're going to make money.

00:03:16.222 --> 00:03:18.184
You know, if you look
at Elon Musk, he thought

00:03:18.184 --> 00:03:20.920
that there was a 90% chance
that his companies would fail.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.004
But he just needed to go and try it.

00:03:23.004 --> 00:03:26.050
When I started helping
entrepreneurs in doing speeches,

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.749
you know, three people
showed up to a free event.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.410
Like, I'm never going to
make money off of this.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.273
It's crazy.

00:03:30.273 --> 00:03:31.404
Entrepreneurs don't have money.

00:03:31.404 --> 00:03:33.999
How am I going to ever
turn this into a business?

00:03:33.999 --> 00:03:36.691
I still needed to just
do it 'cause I loved it.

00:03:36.691 --> 00:03:38.578
And even if it never became a business,

00:03:38.578 --> 00:03:39.924
I would still do it because I have

00:03:39.924 --> 00:03:42.227
the deep passion to helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:44.164
And by doing it over and
over and over and over again,

00:03:44.164 --> 00:03:46.046
you start to maneuver, you
start to figure out ways.

00:03:46.046 --> 00:03:47.480
Hey, I can monetize this.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.419
This is how I can start
making money doing this.

00:03:49.419 --> 00:03:50.298
Money's still important.

00:03:50.298 --> 00:03:51.341
Money feeds everything.

00:03:51.341 --> 00:03:52.875
Money allows me to hire a team.

00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:53.797
Money allows me to grow bigger.

00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:55.617
Money allows me to have a bigger impact.

00:03:55.617 --> 00:03:58.733
But the number one goal for
me is helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:58.733 --> 00:04:00.158
It's what fuels me.

00:04:00.158 --> 00:04:02.407
I could spend all day
helping entrepreneurs

00:04:02.407 --> 00:04:03.940
and not get tired enough
to go to the bathroom

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.767
and not have to eat because
it just fills me up so much.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:09.703
I might crash afterwards, I
might be starving afterwards,

00:04:09.703 --> 00:04:12.682
I might, you know, pass out afterwards,

00:04:12.682 --> 00:04:14.658
but it's that insane drive
that pushes me forward,

00:04:14.658 --> 00:04:17.584
so you need to find the
thing in your business.

00:04:17.584 --> 00:04:20.501
It's the most important
lesson that comes up

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.805
consistently across
successful entrepreneurs

00:04:22.805 --> 00:04:24.987
and athletes and musicians and actors,

00:04:24.987 --> 00:04:27.768
and anybody who's reached
the top in their field.

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.271
You have to love what you're doing.

00:04:29.271 --> 00:04:30.663
Pursue your passion.

00:04:30.663 --> 00:04:33.154
And money's important,
but it's not number one.

00:04:33.154 --> 00:04:34.268
So the question of the day today is,

00:04:34.268 --> 00:04:36.230
I'm curious, what is your number one?

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.314
What's the most important thing

00:04:38.314 --> 00:04:40.124
in your business besides money?

00:04:40.124 --> 00:04:41.420
Super curious to find out.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.786
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:04:42.786 --> 00:04:43.736
I also want want to give a quick

00:04:43.736 --> 00:04:45.453
shout-out to Mohammed Aftab Ali.

00:04:45.453 --> 00:04:47.087
Mohammed, thank you so much for picking up

00:04:47.087 --> 00:04:49.267
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:50.860
I really appreciate the support,

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.814
and I hope you enjoyed your read.

00:04:52.814 --> 00:04:54.416
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:04:54.416 --> 00:04:55.513
I believe in you.

00:04:55.513 --> 00:04:57.417
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:57.417 --> 00:04:59.746
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:59.746 --> 00:05:01.540
Much love and I'll see you again tomorrow

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.128
morning for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:05.128 --> 00:05:07.697
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:07.697 --> 00:05:11.280
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:14.112 --> 00:05:16.069
- Everybody around me, their parents

00:05:16.069 --> 00:05:18.706
were lawyers or investment bankers

00:05:18.706 --> 00:05:22.132
or entrepreneurs, or
they were all involved

00:05:22.132 --> 00:05:24.061
in business and that actually didn't seem

00:05:24.061 --> 00:05:25.899
very much fun to me
growing up, so I thought

00:05:25.899 --> 00:05:28.682
that being an adult's kind of a drag.

00:05:28.682 --> 00:05:29.998
I actually was pretty depressed

00:05:29.998 --> 00:05:31.671
when I graduated from college.

00:05:31.671 --> 00:05:33.756
I mean, I was literally
depressed for six months.

00:05:33.756 --> 00:05:36.717
I woke up at one o'clock in the afternoon

00:05:36.717 --> 00:05:38.624
and laid on a couch and
looked up at the ceiling

00:05:38.624 --> 00:05:40.535
and just said, "Dude,
what am I going to do?"

00:05:40.535 --> 00:05:43.311
And so, with no
inspiration, I just decided,

00:05:43.311 --> 00:05:47.358
you know what, the only thing
I can think of to do right now

00:05:47.358 --> 00:05:50.551
that's going to make me
happy is if I go surfing.

00:05:50.551 --> 00:05:52.038
And so I planned a five-month trip

00:05:52.038 --> 00:05:53.471
around Australia and Indonesia,

00:05:53.471 --> 00:05:56.463
living out of a backpack
and a van at the time.

00:05:56.463 --> 00:05:59.406
If I didn't follow my passion for surfing,

00:05:59.406 --> 00:06:03.469
I would have never had the idea for GoPro.

00:06:03.469 --> 00:06:05.028
- Everything I did, I was following

00:06:05.028 --> 00:06:06.444
something I really cared about,

00:06:06.444 --> 00:06:09.759
something I loved, something
I was passionate about.

00:06:09.759 --> 00:06:11.714
And I kept following that passion,

00:06:11.714 --> 00:06:15.242
whether it was cars,
whether it was anthropology,

00:06:15.242 --> 00:06:17.909
whether it was art, photography.

00:06:19.475 --> 00:06:23.064
And eventually, it led
me to my huge passion,

00:06:23.064 --> 00:06:24.856
my real passion, which was making movies,

00:06:24.856 --> 00:06:26.663
which combined all of those things.

00:06:26.663 --> 00:06:28.475
And I realized that had I gone on

00:06:28.475 --> 00:06:30.571
to get my degree in anthropology,

00:06:30.571 --> 00:06:32.602
I would have probably made
anthropological movies

00:06:32.602 --> 00:06:34.797
in New Guinea or someplace
and eventually been

00:06:34.797 --> 00:06:37.933
on National Geographic and,
you know, The History Channel,

00:06:37.933 --> 00:06:40.908
and been then making features,

00:06:40.908 --> 00:06:43.307
and I'd have done Star Wars just the same.

00:06:43.307 --> 00:06:46.231
If I'd have gone in to Art
Center and become an illustrator,

00:06:46.231 --> 00:06:48.018
I would have probably
started doing animation

00:06:48.018 --> 00:06:50.212
and doing animated films
and making animated things,

00:06:50.212 --> 00:06:51.176
and then ultimately, I would have

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:52.648
gone on and been right where I was.

00:06:52.648 --> 00:06:55.034
So, no matter which route I took,

00:06:55.034 --> 00:06:56.842
because I cared about all of them,

00:06:56.842 --> 00:06:59.250
they all led to the same place.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.588
Had I done what my father
had wished me to do,

00:07:01.588 --> 00:07:05.509
which was to go into the office
equipment business with him,

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:08.587
which I knew I wasn't going
to to do, I knew I hated that,

00:07:08.587 --> 00:07:11.504
my life would have been unpleasant.

00:07:13.242 --> 00:07:17.409
So I think it's very
important not to do what your

00:07:18.288 --> 00:07:21.897
peers think you should do,
not do what your parents

00:07:21.897 --> 00:07:24.151
think you should do, or your teachers,

00:07:24.151 --> 00:07:26.543
but to do what you inside, or even

00:07:26.543 --> 00:07:28.766
your culture thinks, but
do what's inside you.

00:07:28.766 --> 00:07:32.572
- Man, what happened to Pops
when he started a business?

00:07:32.572 --> 00:07:33.856
He failed.

00:07:33.856 --> 00:07:35.511
What happened to Mom and Dad?

00:07:35.511 --> 00:07:36.957
They got a divorce.

00:07:36.957 --> 00:07:38.422
What happened to us?

00:07:38.422 --> 00:07:40.682
We have six different places.

00:07:40.682 --> 00:07:41.843
Was it fun?

00:07:41.843 --> 00:07:43.451
Hell no, it wasn't fun.

00:07:43.451 --> 00:07:45.140
What happened in high school to you?

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.556
Did you play baseball?

00:07:46.556 --> 00:07:48.142
Did you play high school basketball?

00:07:48.142 --> 00:07:49.546
Did you get picked out for football?

00:07:49.546 --> 00:07:50.865
Did you date the girl you liked?

00:07:50.865 --> 00:07:52.160
What was your GPA?

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.563
Who were you in high school?

00:07:53.563 --> 00:07:54.993
Who were you afterwards?

00:07:54.993 --> 00:07:58.006
What makes you think you're
going to make it in life?

00:07:58.006 --> 00:08:00.861
Man, you got to stop selling
this stuff to this guy, man.

00:08:00.861 --> 00:08:01.960
Stop it!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.273
It's getting old.

00:08:03.273 --> 00:08:05.665
Go get that job that you let go of,

00:08:05.665 --> 00:08:09.364
paying you 12 bucks an hour
and part-time get a degree.

00:08:09.364 --> 00:08:11.437
Stop taking these damn risks.

00:08:11.437 --> 00:08:13.224
We're not meant to do something big

00:08:13.224 --> 00:08:15.807
with our lives, simple as that.

00:08:16.676 --> 00:08:17.843
- Are we done?

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:21.443
- I'm done.

00:08:21.443 --> 00:08:23.087
I'm good.

00:08:23.087 --> 00:08:24.170
- Okay, good.

00:08:26.685 --> 00:08:30.384
Pat, I want you to know, this
voice is never going away.

00:08:30.384 --> 00:08:32.208
This voice is always going to be there.

00:08:32.208 --> 00:08:34.610
No matter how much money
you're going to make,

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.555
it's always going to be there.

00:08:36.555 --> 00:08:37.926
The great thing about it is, though,

00:08:37.926 --> 00:08:39.170
every morning you wake up, you have

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:42.090
a choice on which voice to listen to.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:43.235
But I want you to think about a

00:08:43.235 --> 00:08:45.734
completely different thing right now.

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.423
Let's just say you do nothing.

00:08:47.423 --> 00:08:49.092
Let's just say you buy into your fears.

00:08:49.092 --> 00:08:50.401
Let's just say you buy into every

00:08:50.401 --> 00:08:51.893
single thing you're worried about.

00:08:51.893 --> 00:08:53.098
Let's just say you don't make any

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:54.482
decisions to go after your dreams.

00:08:54.482 --> 00:08:56.572
Fast forward 10 years from
now, 20 years from now,

00:08:56.572 --> 00:08:58.941
30 years from now, 40 years from now.

00:08:58.941 --> 00:09:00.753
Let's just say your
funeral's around the corner.

00:09:00.753 --> 00:09:02.537
You have 50 people
there, 100 people there.

00:09:02.537 --> 00:09:04.447
Maybe 200 people show up.

00:09:04.447 --> 00:09:07.324
These are your friends, family
and people that love you.

00:09:07.324 --> 00:09:09.413
So you'll be loved for one generation,

00:09:09.413 --> 00:09:12.574
remembered for two generations
and forgotten after that.

00:09:12.574 --> 00:09:14.545
Is that truly the life you want to live?

00:09:14.545 --> 00:09:16.748
Is that really what you want to do?

00:09:16.748 --> 00:09:19.427
I don't know if that's the
life you really want to live.

00:09:19.427 --> 00:09:21.923
You see, what I've noticed is,
no matter what you ever do,

00:09:21.923 --> 00:09:23.798
you'll have a lot of lonely times.

00:09:23.798 --> 00:09:26.017
You can lie to your family,
you can lie to your friends,

00:09:26.017 --> 00:09:27.868
you can fool the world into realizing

00:09:27.868 --> 00:09:29.337
that why you didn't win was because

00:09:29.337 --> 00:09:31.322
of some challenge that you had to face,

00:09:31.322 --> 00:09:34.121
but there is one person
you can never lie to,

00:09:34.121 --> 00:09:35.839
and that is the man in the mirror.

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:38.878
You can never lie to the
man in the mirror, never.

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:41.072
For the rest of your
life, the man in mirror is

00:09:41.072 --> 00:09:43.417
going to look back at you and say,

00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:46.070
"You did not choose to
go after your dreams."

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.146
And you have to be okay with that.

00:09:48.146 --> 00:09:49.771
Now, what I would like to encourage you

00:09:49.771 --> 00:09:52.534
to do is to make the right choice.

00:09:52.534 --> 00:09:56.058
I encourage you to face your
fears and pursue your dreams.

00:09:56.058 --> 00:09:58.177
Go pursue the dreams that
matter the most to you.

00:09:58.177 --> 00:10:00.450
You only got one shot at this thing here,

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.299
and if it works out, man, it's
going to feel so good for you.

00:10:04.299 --> 00:10:06.086
And if it doesn't, at least you had

00:10:06.086 --> 00:10:08.438
